rnover.",0,25,0,"56634","598","Lost Ball Turnover"],[2,"1:53","2132",53,49,1,3,"Sean Kilpatrick made Three Point Jumper. Assisted by Ge'Lawn Guyn.",1,47,9,"45942","30558","Three Point Jump Shot"],[2,"1:22","41",55,49,1,2,"Shabazz Napier made Jumper.",1,15,14,"51455","20558","JumpShot"],[2,"1:12","2132",55,49,0,0,"Cincinnati  Timeout",0,25,0,null,"579","ShortTimeOut"],[2,"0:51","2132",55,49,0,3,"Ge'Lawn Guyn missed Three Point Jumper.",1,45,11,"56953","30558","Three Point Jump Shot"],[2,"0:51","2132",55,49,0,0,"Shaquille Thomas Offensive Rebound.",0,25,0,"56951","586","Offensive Rebound"],[2,"0:49","2132",55,51,1,2,"Shaquille Thomas made Dunk.",1,26,2,"56951","20574","DunkShot"],[2,"0:49","2132",55,51,0,0,"Cincinnati  Timeout",0,25,0,null,"579","ShortTimeOut"],[2,"0:48","41",55,51,0,0,"Lasan Kromah Turnover.",0,25,0,"46103","598","Lost Ball Turnover"],[2,"0:48","2132",55,51,0,0,"Ge'Lawn Guyn Steal.",0,25,0,"56953","607","Steal"],[2,"0:42","41",55,51,0,0,"Foul on Niels Giffey.",0,25,0,"53045","519","PersonalFoul"],[2,"0:42","2132",55,52,1,1,"Sean Kilpatrick made Free Throw.",1,null,null,"45942","540","MadeFreeThrow"],[2,"0:42","2132",55,53,1,1,"Sean Kilpatrick made Free Throw.",1,null,null,"45942","540","MadeFreeThrow"],[2,"0:31","2132",55,53,0,0,"Foul on Sean Kilpatrick.",0,25,0,"45942","519","PersonalFoul"],[2,"0:31","41",56,53,1,1,"Ryan Boatright made Free Throw.",1,null,null,"56634","540","MadeFreeThrow"],[2,"0:31","41",57,53,1,1,"Ryan Boatright made Free Throw.",1,null,null,"56634","540","MadeFreeThrow"],[2,"0:14","2132",57,56,1,3,"Jermaine Sanders made Three Point Jumper. Assisted by Sean Kilpatrick.",1,22,24,"56954","30558","Three Point Jump Shot"],[2,"0:12","41",57,56,0,0,"Connecticut  Timeout",0,25,0,null,"579","ShortTimeOut"],[2,"0:11","2132",57,56,0,0,"Foul on Titus Rubles.",0,25,0,"61850","519","PersonalFoul"],[2,"0:11","41",58,56,1,1,"Shabazz Napier made Free Throw.",1,null,null,"51455","540","MadeFreeThrow"],[2,"0:11","41",58,56,0,1,"Shabazz Napier missed Free Throw.",1,null,null,"51455","540","MadeFreeThrow"],[2,"0:11","2132",58,56,0,0,"Justin Jackson Defensive Rebound.",0,25,0,"51235","587","Defensive Rebound"],[2,"0:01","2132",58,56,0,2,"Sean Kilpatrick missed Layup.",1,22,3,"45942","20572","LayUpShot"],[2,"0:01","2132",58,56,0,0,"Cincinnati Deadball Team Rebound.",0,25,0,null,"449","Dead Ball Rebound"],[2,"0:00",null,58,56,0,0,"End of Game",0,50,-5,null,"402","End Game"]],"wp":[],"article":{"headline":"Shabazz Napier clutch as No. 21 UConn edges No. 13 Cincy","description":"Shabazz Napier hit a free throw with 11.1 seconds left as No. 21 Connecticut held off 13th-ranked Cincinnati 58-56 Friday night to advance to the American Athletic Conference tournament final.","type":"Recap","source":"Associated Press","published":"2014-03-15T12:10:55Z","story":"<p>MEMPHIS, Tenn. -- Sitting at home in the postseason a year ago is something that stuck with the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/team/_/id/41/connecticut-huskies\">Connecticut Huskies</a>, and they are busy making up for lost time.</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/player/_/id/51455/shabazz-napier\">Shabazz Napier</a> hit a free throw with 11.1 seconds left as No. 21 Connecticut held off 13th-ranked Cincinnati 58-56 Friday night to advance to the American Athletic Conference tournament final.</p>\n<p>The Huskies (26-7) were barred from last year's tournament in the Big East and the NCAA tournament, and now they are back in their first tournament final since 2011 when they won the national championship. They will play another former Big East team for the inaugural American tournament title Saturday in No. 5 Louisville, a 94-65 winner over Houston.</p>\n<p>\"Oh, it feels great, but it started last year when we couldn't perform in a conference tournament or go to the NCAA tournament,\" UConn coach Kevin Ollie said. \"Those guys still played for our great university, and they stayed loyal to the program.\"</p>\n<p>Cincinnati (27-6) lost to UConn for the second straight time and missed out on its second tournament final in three years.</p>\n<p>The Bearcats had the ball and a final chance with Napier defending <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/player/_/id/45942/sean-kilpatrick\">Sean Kilpatrick</a>, but the Cincinnati senior missed a layup with 3 seconds left. Cincinnati couldn't get another shot off before the buzzer.</p>\n<p>Napier said he tried to cut off Kilpatrick, sending the Cincinnati guard back to the middle where the layup was contested.</p>\n<p>\"I thought it was going to go down, but he put too much spin on it and it went out the other way,\" Napier said. \"My big guys definitely was smacking the ball up in the air, just in case one of them guys was trying to grab it and that buzzer sounded off.\"</p>\n<p>Cincinnati coach Mick Cronin said the only empty possession the Bearcats had in the final 3 minutes was the missed layup at the end. Asked if the net might have been hit on Kilpatrick's shot to draw a goaltending call, Cronin said he's worried about Sunday and the NCAA tournament bracket announcement.</p>\n<p>\"I'm not tall enough to see stuff like that,\" Cronin said. \"You really think that they're going to call that for Cincinnati? What games you been watching all year.\"</p>\n<p>Napier finished with 15 points. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/player/_/id/56635/deandre-daniels\">DeAndre Daniels</a> had 14 points and nine rebounds. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/player/_/id/56634/ryan-boatright\">Ryan Boatright</a> added 13, and Niles Giffey had 11 on 4-of-5 shooting, including 3 of 4 from 3-point range for UConn. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/player/_/id/66679/amida-brimah\">Amida Brimah</a> had seven rebounds and four blocks, three in the second half.</p>\n<p>Kilpatrick finished with 14 points for Cincinnati, while <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/player/_/id/51235/justin-jackson\">Justin Jackson</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/player/_/id/56954/jermaine-sanders\">Jermaine Sanders</a> had 10 each. Jackson grabbed eight rebounds. Sanders' 3 with 12.2 seconds left from the top of the key set the stage for the final thrilling seconds.</p>\n<p>This was the tiebreaker between the teams after each won on home court this season. It also became the sixth straight game between these teams were decided by six or fewer points, and they've split with three each. This was their first game on a neutral court since UConn knocked the Bearcats out of the NCAA tournament on its way to the national title.</p>\n<p>\"It seems like every time we play Cincy, it comes down to a one-possession game,\" Ollie said. \"They're well-coached. They play so hard, and I thought we just stood up to them. We stayed in the middle of the ring and kept throwing punches.\"</p>\n<p>UConn shot better from 3-point range connecting on 53.8 percent (7 of 13) including 4 of 5 in the second half. Overall, the Huskies shot 44 percent. Meanwhile Cincinnati was limited to 38 percent.</p>\n<p>The big difference was at the free-throw line where UConn converted 15 of 18 with 11 of 13 coming in the second half compared to Cincinnati who went 6 of 13, hitting all two attempts in the second half. Cronin noted they didn't take those two free throws until the final 2 minutes.</p>\n<p>Cincinnati built its 31-27 halftime lead to as much as seven a couple times, the last at 39-32. The Huskies scored 11 of the next 13 points, including nine straight, and Boatright's 3-pointer put them ahead 43-41 with 9:32 left for their first lead since 23-21. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/player/_/id/66971/troy-caupain\">Troy Caupain</a> ended a nearly 6-minute scoring drought for Cincinnati with a layup with 8:10 remaining only to see Boatright hit his second straight 3-pointer.</p>\n<p>The Huskies turned up the defense themselves and forced Cincinnati into two shot clock violations.</p>\n<p>Sanders ended a 17-2 run by UConn with a 3-pointer with 3:24 to go, the first of three he hit down the stretch.</p>\n\n\n\n\n","images":[{"url":"https://a.espncdn.com/photo/2014/0314/ncb_a_deandredaniels_ms_576x324.jpg","caption":null,"credit":"AP Photo/Mark Humphrey","width":576,"height":324}]},"videos":[],"news":[],"source":{"summary":true,"boxscore":"full","playByPlay":"full"}}